// Command node implements Maelstrom's Kafka-style log service.
//
// The service keeps a set of append-only logs, one per string key. Each
// message appended to a log ("send") is given a unique, monotonically
// increasing offset in that log, starting at zero. "poll" hands back every
// message at or after a given offset, "commit_offsets" records how far
// clients have read, and "list_committed_offsets" reads that back.
//
// All state lives on a single leader node -- the first node in Maelstrom's
// node ID list, which every node agrees on -- so that appends and polls are
// strongly consistent: an acknowledged send is never lost, never moves, and
// always reads back the same value at the same offset. Other nodes, if there
// are any, relay requests to the leader and have the leader answer the client
// directly, which keeps node-to-node messages small. The log lives in memory,
// which is fine for the lifetime of a Maelstrom test.
package main
